        "category": "ancestry",
        "source": "Bad Eden (2024 rules)",
        "tags": [],
        "description": {
          "value": "<div data-ft-phase5-vocab-scrub=\"v1\" style=\"display:none\"></div><p><strong>Human.</strong> Normalized Bad Eden ancestry root.</p><p>Select one heritage separately when building the character: <strong>Cro-Magnon, Denisovan, Florensis, Neanderthal</strong>.</p><p>This root grants the shared Human core trait package and preserves live UUID compatibility for existing feature items.</p><p><em>\u201cHumanity is not special. It\u2019s just stubborn enough to keep moving when reality begs it to stop.\u201d</em></p><p><strong>Adaptive.</strong> 1/Soma Break, when you fail a check, you can choose to succeed instead.</p><p><strong>Tenacious.</strong> While you have 1 Integrity, you reroll the lowest die on one check of your choice each round (declare before rolling).</p><p><strong>Lineage Memory.</strong> Choose one human lineage (Cro-Magnon, Denisovan, Florensis, Neanderthal). Your lineage grants Tier powers as you level.</p>",
          "chat": ""
        },
