    {
      "name": "Human Heritage: Cro-Magnon",
      "type": "feat",
      "img": "art/bbttcc/GOTTGAIT/GOTTGAIT%20Token/ezeren_shadow_courier.png",
      "system": {
        "category": "technique",
        "source": "Bad Eden (2024 rules)",
        "tags": [],
        "description": {
          "value": "<div data-ft-phase5-vocab-scrub=\"v1\" style=\"display:none\"></div><p><strong>New Heritage (v2).</strong> Cro-Magnon replaces Erectus in the Human heritage lineup.</p><p><em>\u201cHumanity is the species that keeps walking even when the map says \u2018stop.\u2019\u201d</em></p><p><strong>Human (Cro-Magnon).</strong> You are not a fantasy human. You are the cognitive, symbolic, cooperative inheritance of the lineage that first painted ancestors on cave walls, buried its dead with flowers, and traded ochre across a continent it had no map for.</p><p>Where Neanderthal is <em>strength</em> and Florensis is <em>reach</em>, Cro-Magnon is <em>pattern</em>. Language, ritual, coalition. You are the human branch that kept explaining things until the explanation started working.</p><h3>Traits</h3><ul><li><p><strong>Creature Type.</strong> Humanoid.</p></li><li><p><strong>Size.</strong> Medium.</p></li><li><p><strong>Speed.</strong> 6 squares</p></li><li><p><strong>Lineage Lean.</strong> Your lineage leans toward <strong>MND (Mind)</strong> or <strong>PRE (Presence)</strong>\u2014expressed through Tier powers.</p></li></ul><h3>Core: Stubborn Spark</h3><p>At creation you gain <strong>Stubborn Spark</strong> (Adaptive, Tenacious, Lineage Memory).</p><h3>Cro-Magnon Tier Powers</h3><p>You gain Tier I at creation, then Tier II (5), Tier III (11), Tier IV (17). Cro-Magnon powers emphasize: <em>Symbolic Thought</em> (ritual and language sensitivity), <em>Coalition Instinct</em> (cooperation bonuses with allies), <em>Tool Mind</em> (improvisational tool use), and <em>Narrative Memory</em> (lore retention that persists across generations).</p>",
          "chat": ""
        },
